course: dictionary
lesson: 210
title: Alert: watching, warning and warning someone
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Alert has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one. Its main meaning is watching and listening carefully, awake and ready to act. «Be alert when you cross the road.» Here it means keep your eyes and ears open.
explain: Alert can also be a noun, meaning a warning. «The phone sent a weather alert about the storm.» The clues are phone, weather and storm, so an alert is a message that tells you about danger.
explain: Alert can be a verb too, meaning to warn someone so they can act. «The lifeguard alerted us to the strong current.» Ask yourself: what would fit here? Warned would fit, so alerted means warned.
fact: Alert means watching and listening carefully, awake and ready to notice danger or act quickly.
fact: As a noun, an alert is a warning signal or message about danger or something important.
fact: As a verb, to alert someone means to warn them so they can act.
fact: «On high alert» means ready and watching for danger.
fact: Phones, computers and authorities send alerts, for example about storms, floods and fires.
exercise: «Be alert when you cross the road.» What does alert mean here? | Wearing bright colours | Half asleep and yawning | Running very fast | *Watching and listening carefully
exercise: «The phone sent a weather alert about the storm.» What is an alert in this sentence? | A kind of phone case | A game to play | *A warning message about danger | A type of cloud
exercise: «The lifeguard alerted us to the strong current.» What does alerted mean? | *Warned us so we could act | Sang a song to us | Ignored us | Put us to sleep
test: «During a hurricane warning, the family listens to official alerts.» What are the official alerts? | Recipes for dinner | Bedtime stories | Music for dancing | *Warning messages about danger
test: «An exciting game keeps the brain alert, so it is harder to fall asleep.» Which word means nearly the same as alert here? | *Awake and ready | Angry | Silent | Sleepy
exam: «Stay alert near water.» Which meaning fits best? | Very tired | *Keep your eyes and ears open | Sleepy and calm | Loud and cheerful
